is":{"language":null,"source":"anilist","spoiler":false,"text":"Not wanting to lose, Yi-rang orchestrates a collapse in the middle of a relay race even though she's on the verge of giving up her dream of becoming an athlete. At the same time, Soo-min transfers in from Seoul and Cheol-soo, who dreams of becoming a scientist, come into her life. They are all immature but they are in the midst of youthful aspiration.\n\nWith this warm-hearted animation, Han Hye-jin-I and Ahn Jae-hoon encourage Yi-rang's dreams and portray the fantasy and flutter of adolescence through encounters with good people. Set in the '80s and '90s, an old umbrella and a railroad crossing the downtown in the film is the stuff that reminds us of our lost past, evoking a reminiscence in the audience of that which is vanished.\n\nIt is a way of evoking the real \"dreams\" that we have lost in this modern society where a rapid capitalization is progressing.\n\n(Source: Hancinema)"},"tags":[{"name":"Female Protagonist","rank":20,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Coming of Age","rank":20,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Rural","rank":20,"spoiler":false},{"name":"School","rank":20,"spoiler":false}],"titles":{"display":"So-jjoong-han Nam-eui Ggoom","english":null,"native":"소중한 날의 꿈","romaji":"So-jjoong-han Nam-eui Ggoom","synonyms":[{"language":"zh","source":"bangumi","value":"珍贵日子的梦想"},{"language":null,"source":"bangumi","value":"珍爱之日的梦"},{"language":null,"source":"bangumi","value":"Green Days"}]},"trailer":null,"visibility":"general"}